name: --help prints the option list, exit 0
clause: s31_1_c_2
clause: s31_12_i_1
command: gencat
namespace: none
# The bug-reporting lines name the distribution: an identity string (Q3 of plan/utilities.md).
env: LC_ALL=C.UTF-8
normalise: standard output.\n\nFor bug reporting instructions, please see:\n<https://bugs.launchpad.net/ubuntu/+source/glibc/+bugs>.\n => standard output.\n
arg: --help
status: exit 0
stdout:
| Usage: gencat [OPTION...] -o OUTPUT-FILE [INPUT-FILE]...
| \x20 or:  gencat [OPTION...] [OUTPUT-FILE [INPUT-FILE]...]
| Generate message catalog.
|
| \x20 -H, --header=NAME          Create C header file NAME containing symbol
| \x20                            definitions
| \x20     --new                  Do not use existing catalog, force new output file
| \x20                          \x20
| \x20 -o, --output=NAME          Write output to file NAME
| \x20 -?, --help                 Give this help list
| \x20     --usage                Give a short usage message
| \x20 -V, --version              Print program version
|
| Mandatory or optional arguments to long options are also mandatory or optional
| for any corresponding short options.
|
| If INPUT-FILE is -, input is read from standard input.  If OUTPUT-FILE
| is -, output is written to standard output.
stderr:
